WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Why can you squash air but not water?

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:09.980
Gas particles have big gaps between them. Push, and they move closer.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:15.060
Liquid particles already touch. There is nowhere left to go.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:21.013
That is why gas can be squeezed into a tank, but water hardly squashes at all.
